# Format: <name> <upstream-commit-or-tag> <license-id> <upstream-url>
#
# One uncommented line per vendor/<name>/ tree, and `<name>` must equal the
# directory name. The four fields are machine-read by check_opensource_purity.rb;
# everything else on this page is a comment. A commented line is NOT a pin.
#
# PERMISSIVE ONLY, as in every other vendored tree in the OSS drop. OFL-1.1 is
# on check_opensource_purity.rb's PERMISSIVE_LICENCE_IDS allowlist: it permits
# unrestricted commercial use, embedding and redistribution of the font bytes,
# it imposes nothing on the software that renders them, and the only obligations
# it carries - keep the copyright notice with the bytes, do not sell the font on
# its own - are satisfied by vendor/inter/LICENSE.txt sitting next to the files.
# Inter declares NO Reserved Font Name (its copyright line is a bare
# "Copyright (c) 2016-2018 The Inter Project Authors", with no "with Reserved
# Font Name" clause), so the subsets below keep the upstream family name.
#
# The BYTES HERE ARE DERIVED, not a copy of the upstream release: two
# unicode-range subsets of one variable file, both axes intact. That is the same
# shape as Local/vendor/sqlite, which vendors the amalgamation rather than the
# upstream source tree. vendor/inter/DERIVATION.md carries the upstream sha256
# and the exact command, so the bytes can be reproduced from the pin.

